Grammar

    0 $accept: S $end

    1 S: E

    2 E: ID
    3  | ID LPAREN E RPAREN
    4  | E PLUS ID


Terminals, with rules where they appear

    $end (0) 0
    error (256)
    ID <sValue> (258) 2 3 4
    PLUS (259) 4
    LPAREN (260) 3
    RPAREN (261) 3


Nonterminals, with rules where they appear

    $accept (7)
        on left: 0
    S (8)
        on left: 1
        on right: 0
    E <sValue> (9)
        on left: 2 3 4
        on right: 1 3 4


State 0

    0 $accept: • S $end

    ID  shift, and go to state 1

    S  go to state 2
    E  go to state 3


State 1

    2 E: ID •
    3  | ID • LPAREN E RPAREN

    LPAREN  shift, and go to state 4

    $default  reduce using rule 2 (E)


State 2

    0 $accept: S • $end

    $end  shift, and go to state 5


State 3

    1 S: E •
    4 E: E • PLUS ID

    PLUS  shift, and go to state 6

    $default  reduce using rule 1 (S)


State 4

    3 E: ID LPAREN • E RPAREN

    ID  shift, and go to state 1

    E  go to state 7


State 5

    0 $accept: S $end •

    $default  accept


State 6

    4 E: E PLUS • ID

    ID  shift, and go to state 8


State 7

    3 E: ID LPAREN E • RPAREN
    4  | E • PLUS ID

    PLUS    shift, and go to state 6
    RPAREN  shift, and go to state 9


State 8

    4 E: E PLUS ID •

    $default  reduce using rule 4 (E)


State 9

    3 E: ID LPAREN E RPAREN •

    $default  reduce using rule 3 (E)
